WEBVTT

00:36:59.188 --> 00:37:00.625
kids would throw rocks at you.

00:37:00.649 --> 00:37:02.675
But it was a creative
tension, ultimately,

00:37:02.699 --> 00:37:04.477
and it was something we could handle.

00:37:04.501 --> 00:37:07.287
And the vision of America
as the universal nation

00:37:07.311 --> 00:37:09.412
was realized in some large measure.

00:37:09.436 --> 00:37:11.216
I think that's still happening today.

00:37:11.240 --> 00:37:13.191
I was in Nebraska yesterday,

00:37:13.215 --> 00:37:16.577
and I had dinner with
about 15 folks in Nebraska.

00:37:16.601 --> 00:37:18.672
They were all white
except one Latina woman,

00:37:18.696 --> 00:37:21.484
who was a small-business owner
in their small town.

00:37:21.508 --> 00:37:25.211
And she said, "I never had a home,
I had to leave home when I was 14.

00:37:25.235 --> 00:37:26.968
But you people have given me a home,

00:37:26.992 --> 00:37:29.369
and I love you for the way
you've made me feel.

00:37:29.393 --> 00:37:32.432
And in the last few years,
I've just had to turn off Twitter,